+# SIGBLEND band (K-sprint, 2026-09-27) — how to re-create it from the release
+
+Inference-only; no training beyond the recipe-A members and their held-out twins.
+
+1. Train the recipe-A members and the five held-out twins (REPRODUCE.md 1.4 / 1.5) and fit the shipped band
+   (`submit_fno/fit_band.py --ckpt <all-data members> --err-ckpt <twins> --alpha 0.80 --band-p 0.45 --centre-alpha 0
+   --fill-unscored --inflate 1.39`)  -> `band_r38_a080_c0_fill.npz`.
+2. Dump the twins' fields on `val_unseen` (8 trajectories no twin has seen): `python Track_1/sigblend/dump_twins.py <dump.npz>`
+   (edit `U` / `out` paths; GPU or CPU).
+3. `B_DUMP=<dump.npz> K0_BAND=<band_r38_a080_c0_fill.npz> K0_INFL=1.29 K0_NB=16 python Track_1/sigblend/make_k0_band.py <outdir>`
+   (needs `Track_1/sps9.py` on the path: run it from `Track_1/sigblend/` with `PYTHONPATH=Track_1`). It prints the
+   leave-one-trajectory-out read and writes `band_k0_sigblend_lam{0.3,0.5,0.7}.npz` + `.json`
+   (q per channel, log kappa per frame, the T1 `EBAND` literal and the T2 `SIGPOW` exponents).
+4. Build with `RPDE_BAND=<band_k0_sigblend_lam0.5.npz> RPDE_SHIP_EBAND='<literal>' RPDE_SHIP_SIGPOW='(<u>, <v>)'
+   RPDE_SHIP_SMALL_GRAPH=False RPDE_SHIP_JOINT_GAIN=True RPDE_SHIP_WARM_TAILS=True RPDE_SHIP_PIN_OUT=128
+   RPDE_SHIP_BATCH_CAP=56 RPDE_SHIP_ARENA_STEPS=1024` plus the recipe-A knob sets (job script: `jobs/rp_k27_final.sh`
+   in the K-sprint scratch, copied next to this file).
+
+Formula evaluated by the package (T1: `_fno.predict_fno` band_gpu + EBAND "mult"; T2: `submission.py` SIGPOW):
+
+    half = base' * clip(sigma/sigma_ref, .3, 3)^p' * (sigma + 1e-8)^(lam * q_c)
+    base' = base^(1-lam) * kappa_{t,c}^lam,  p' = (1-lam) * 0.45,  lam = 0.5,  q = (0.4847, 0.4907)
+
+Traps: a SIGBLEND npz in a package that does not apply the sigma-power factor is ~3x too wide; T1 EBAND needs the GPU-band
+path for every N, so the small batch-1 graph must be off.
